1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,794
Every line of this invoice is right. The total is one cent off. And every test passes.

2
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:18,861
This is how old business software dies. Someone rewrites it, nobody can say what the old one really did, and

3
00:00:18,861 --> 00:00:25,322
the bugs that slip through are business bugs. Parity proves the new app does the same thing, field by field.

4
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:38,421
You record someone using the old app and talking. Meta's models read the narration and every field on every frame, and the business rules

5
00:00:38,421 --> 00:00:46,442
come out in plain language, each with its evidence. Code checks every formula against the recorded values. An expert accepts them in a click.

6
00:00:55,400 --> 00:01:00,384
Muse Code builds the web app from the accepted rules. Parity replays the

7
00:01:00,384 --> 00:01:05,368
same invoice on it: eight of eight fields equal, first try, for forty-six cents.

8
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:21,814
When a rebuild rounds the taxes too early, Parity names the field: sixty-nine twenty-one before,

9
00:01:21,814 --> 00:01:28,227
sixty-nine twenty-two after. AI never decides what the same means. The comparison is plain code.

10
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:41,924
On FrontAccounting, an app nobody here wrote, Parity fuzzes the rebuild against the live app, shrinks the

11
00:01:41,924 --> 00:01:48,447
difference to one line, and hands Muse Code the cases around it. One repair, thirty-six cents, parity.

12
00:01:55,400 --> 00:02:00,499
The proof stays. Every pull request replays it, with no model call. A change

13
00:02:00,499 --> 00:02:05,598
that rounds the taxes per line fails its check, and the comment names the cent.

14
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:22,233
Muse Spark computer use explores the app and turns screens nobody recorded into tests. Migration mode goes screen

15
00:02:22,233 --> 00:02:29,067
by screen: customers, items and invoices, on records read through the old app's own forms, each one proved.

16
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:39,739
Nothing leaves your machine unless you send it. Every model call is

17
00:02:39,739 --> 00:02:44,078
in the send log, with its cost. The whole build cost eighteen dollars.

18
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:55,674
Parity. Record it once, prove it forever. Open source.
